    "faq": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "start": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Which product should I start with?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>If you are new to supplements, start with one. For most people that is a multivitamin or a hydration powder, depending on what is missing from your day. The How to choose page walks through it in a few minutes, and you can email us if you are still unsure.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "medication": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "I take medication. Is this safe for me?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We cannot answer that for you. Some ingredients, including ashwagandha and turmeric, can interact with medications. Please check with your pharmacist or doctor before starting anything new, and bring the label with you.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "notice": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "When will I notice anything?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>It depends on the product and on you. Electrolytes work within the hour. Creatine takes a few weeks to build up. Multivitamins and adaptogens are usually a matter of weeks, and some people notice nothing obvious, which is normal. We do not promise a feeling.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "vegan": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are your products vegan and gluten-free?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Most are. Each product page lists this under What's in it, and the label is always the final word. The whey protein is not vegan; the plant protein is.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "storage": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How should I store them?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Cool, dry, out of direct sun, lid closed. The bathroom cabinet is usually too humid for powders. Capsules are fine in a kitchen cupboard.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
